# Publish, Studio finish, affiliate, social

Full rules: `STUDIO_PLAYBOOK.md` §9–§12.

- **Channel:** `@HistoryOfScienceYT` (`UCXp7HkBIl1LgaznXuZHJyRg`) only. `CHANNEL_META.json` lists the channels never to touch.
- **Upload:** Data API package: `npm run youtube:package -- --package <…> --video <mp4> --dry-run` first. Private + `publishAt`, explicit `privacyStatus` and `madeForKids`, altered content: yes.
- **One video = one upload:**
  - never swap a file on a live id (no Studio Replace); never re-upload a public idea;
  - a recut gets a new id, and the old one goes private (not deleted).
- **Long:** normal publish, Thursday 18:00 UK, never a Premiere. Test & Compare with 3 thumbs, end screen, captions from the script. Pinned comment: `07_Content-Ops/scripts/update-pinned-comment.ts --create --video <id> --question "…?"`, then pin it in Studio.
- **Short:** Studio Related → the long it promotes. No pinned comment, zero `/go/`.
- **Contract checks (paste the PASS):** `cd 07_Content-Ops && npm run lint:package` before any upload/schedule/metadata change; `npm run channel:audit` (0 errors) after every Studio session and every Monday. Shorts are declared first in `10_Shorts/SHORTS_RELEASE.json`.
- **Studio settings on every video** (`STUDIO_PLAYBOOK.md` §9, 30 Sep 2026; HOS 004 went up as Made for Kids):
  - **Audience "not made for kids"** (channel default too). Re-read Audience and Visibility after **every** save; one setting per save.
  - Scheduled with Premiere off, notify subscribers on; altered/synthetic content **Yes** (the API can't read it: confirm by eye in Studio); category Education; English (UK); captions `.srt`; comments on (hold inappropriate).
  - Longs: Test & Compare, end screen, **2 cards** (not in the first minute), the "How Did We Discover…? | History of Science" playlist, pinned comment. After publish, point the older longs' end screens at the new film.
  - Screenshot Visibility, Audience, T&C, end screen and cards; record them in `production-status.md`.
  - **Every video, long or Short, old or new:** paid promotion No; video and title/description language English (UK); education fields (concept overview; Academic system **England**, never another country; closest level to 14–16 and the GCSE subject if Studio offers them); automatic places off; 5–8 tags on this video's own subject only, **never another channel's name**; no hashtag titles from vidIQ; a Short never reuses a title the long is testing. Times in UK with UTC beside them, Studio time zone London. New Short ideas are checked against the **live** Shorts page.
- **Title-only fixes:** `07_Content-Ops/scripts/retitle-videos.ts` (dry run first, Ben OK).
- **Studio-only jobs** go through desktop Studio CDP (`00_Brand/Channel-Setup/audits/start_studio_chrome_cdp.sh`). Never Replace.
- **Affiliate:** only on a long that names the product in VO or on screen; one product per film; never invent ASINs; never commit the Amazon tag.
- **Social (Buffer / Showrunner only):**
  - **TikTok:** Buffer only (Ben, 5 Oct 2026). Direct uploads stay paused (`TikTok/TIKTOK_UPLOAD_BLOCK.json`): no direct uploads, retries or "test one".
  - Post HOS social via **Buffer** using **`BUFFER_HOS_API_KEY`** (HOS Buffer org). Never the Orbit Buffer org. Never the Buffer connector (Orbit-only).
  - YouTube stays in Studio / YouTube API — Buffer does not upload to YouTube.
  - Shorts only on Buffer (TikTok / Instagram / Facebook when connected). **Long films are never cross-posted via Buffer.**
  - Captions: Facebook → direct YouTube link to the long; TikTok / Instagram → "Full film on YouTube, link in bio".
  - Instagram `@historyofscienceyt`: each Short at most once per platform, never before its long is public (`social/uniqueness.py`). Never post to an Orbit account or the Orbit Facebook Page.
  - **HOS Threads posting stops** (no Threads channel in HOS Buffer; do not add one without Ben).
  - Keep `social/uniqueness.py` and `social/destination.py`. Brand bios and `TikTok/TIKTOK_UPLOAD_BLOCK.json` stay in place.
  - Do not revive archived `live_shorts_to_*` / launchd plists under `_archive/00_Brand/Channel-Setup/`.
